{"id":"wikibooks:veal-stock","verdict":"keep","reason":"Keep the complete white-stock recipe; the alternative brown-stock method was concatenated after freezing the stock.","recipes":[{"source":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook%3AVeal_Stock","status":"fixed","ingredients":["5 lb veal shank, sawn into 2-inch lengths","2 lb veal shin bones, sawn into 2-inch lengths","1 lb veal marrow bones","2 lb chicken carcasses","½ lb (2 medium) onions, in medium dice","4 oz (2 medium) carrots, peeled and in medium dice","4 oz (2 stalks) celery with leaves, sliced","4 oz (2 medium) leeks including 2 inches of the green part, sliced and washed thoroughly","1 large clove garlic, crushed","10 sprigs fresh parsley, bruised","2 sprigs fresh thyme","1 bay leaf","½ tsp whole black peppercorns","1 tsp salt"],"steps":["Put the veal and chicken bones into a stock pot, and add enough water to cover the bones by 2 inches.","Bring to a simmer over medium heat, and skim off any scum as it forms. Simmer for 30 minutes—do not boil.","Add the vegetables and seasonings and simmer for 6 to 8 hours.","Remove the bones with tongs or a spider and strain into another container. Rinse the pot.","Strain the stock back into the stock pot through a double layer of damp cheesecloth.","Place the pot in a sink of cold water and allow to cool. Refrigerate.","Remove from the refrigerator and lift off the layer of fat.","Divide into suitably sized portions and freeze."]}]}
